.nh
.TH "PB-SEND-STATUS" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-send-status - Inspect a file transfer


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb send status <transfer-id> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Show one outgoing transfer: its delivery progress and receipt. --on is required: name the
machine the files were sent to. Delivered to the receiver is not the same as verified by it;
only the receiver's verified receipt means done.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for status

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON

.PP
\fB--on\fP=""
	machine the files were sent to, by name or ID (required)

.PP
\fB--session\fP=""
	terminal session ID for destination context


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb send status transfer_abc --on laptop
  pb send status transfer_abc --on laptop --json
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-send(1)\fP
